            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Bengali for to postpone, then the Bengali for to chase up."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: প্রতিশ্রুতি",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "প্রতিশ্রুতি — prôtishruti — \"a promise; a pledge\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "নেতা যদি প্রতিশ্রুতি না রাখেন, তাহলে আমরা ভোট দেব না। netā jôdi prôtishruti nā rākhen, tāhôle āmrā bhoṭ debô nā. If the leader doesn't keep his promise, we won't vote for him."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "প্রতিশ্রুতি (prôtishruti) is Sanskrit pratiśruti, a promise (Monier-Williams), from prati-śru 'to listen to, to agree'. It is given with দেওয়া and kept with রাখা."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
